# Accepted findings of scripts/static.sh: tool|check|file|message, no line numbers; a clang row has a TAB and the reason it is accepted: `read` is shown by the code, `unproven` is not (grep unproven). Regenerate with scripts/static.sh --update-baseline (the reasons are kept).
clang|core.BitwiseShift|src/agg/pred.c|Right operand is negative in left shift [core.BitwiseShift]	read: n is a row count >= 0 and the branch is taken for w < (n + 63) / 64, where n - w * 64 is in 1..63
